      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Linguistic standardization in high-level communication helps maintain corporate reputation and stakeholder confidence because it conveys professionalism and precision. Non-standard dialects, while culturally rich, can be perceived as unprofessional or lack clarity and simplicity, thereby risking misunderstandings. For a Fortune 500 firm, presenting a unified brand voice through Standard Professional English fosters strong, clear, and authoritative messaging, essential for investor relations and global markets. By ensuring executives communicate with linguistic consistency, the company reinforces stability and reliability in uncertain economic climates.",
      "source": "target",
